            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to unload, then the Hindi for to put on board."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सराय",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सराय — sarāy — \"an inn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पहले मुसाफ़िर सराय में रुकते थे। pahle musāfir sarāy meṁ rukte the. In the old days, travellers used to stop at an inn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सराय (sarāy) is usually traced to Persian sarāy, \"a large house, a palace\", which also named the walled inns built along the old trade roads; many towns still have a lane or a quarter called सराय."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
